Experimental Hardware: Gulfport Plasma Confinement Demonstrator
Primary Operating Principle
Plasma confinement is achieved exclusively through passive toroidal inversion geometry. The ascending gas jet is conditioned by the water toroid primary driver and focused by the threaded axial column, producing plasma at the nozzle. Geometric inversion causes the plasma to fold back downward along the outer boundary, creating a self-confining loop. The plasma inverts and moves back down, confining itself. Zero magnetic input. Zero electrical input. Gas stove burner only.

Operational History
The assembly has maintained stable operation for approximately five years. Permanent donut magnets were present for a period of approximately six to seven months within that operational history only. The device demonstrated consistent plasma confinement and characteristic emission behavior both prior to magnet introduction and following their removal. Current configuration contains zero magnetic components. The magnet period represents a minority variable within the total operational record — the dominant operational condition across the full five years has been zero magnets.

