The water toroid replaces the cast iron enstrophy containment sleeve as the density boundary layer. Water is diamagnetic, has high dielectric constant, and self-organizes into the toroidal geometry purely by container shape and gravity. The gas jet ascending through the center interacts with the water toroid boundary before being focused — a passive geometric inversion field requiring no external maintenance. Graphite ablation behavior and blue plasma emission confirmed in this configuration, establishing material independence of the confinement mechanism.

